PTLib 2.12-beta10 (OPAL stack): give the generated revision header a revision

src/Makefile generates revision.h from revision.h.in by extracting a number out
of the file's Subversion $Revision$ keyword.  These sources are consumed from a
git mirror, where that keyword is never expanded, so the extraction yields
nothing and the generated header reads `#define SVN_REVISION` with no value -
which makes PProcess::GetLibVersion() in osutils.cxx a syntax error.

Seeding the keyword with 0 makes the generated header read
`#define SVN_REVISION 0`, which is what the retained source tree that produced
this project's installed PTLib carried.  0 rather than an invented number: the
value only reaches PProcess::GetLibVersion()'s "(svn:%u)" suffix, and a git
mirror has no Subversion revision to report honestly.

Applies to: 10503462abe31a6c288a39f6f894a5ceb367abbc (branch v2_12)
Upstream:   https://git.code.sf.net/p/opalvoip/ptlib

diff --git a/revision.h.in b/revision.h.in
index 15da936..6ae38ec 100644
--- a/revision.h.in
+++ b/revision.h.in
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
  *
  * Contributor(s): ______________________________________.
  *
- * $Revision$
+ * $Revision: 0 $
  * $Author$
  * $Date$
  */
